<!--
    Launcher icon, foreground layer.

    A mosque in silhouette: dome, cornice, two minarets, a crescent finial.
    Chosen over the usual crescent-and-star because a solid silhouette still
    reads at 48dp, where thin points turn to mush, and because every second
    app on the phone is already a crescent and a star.

    Two golds rather than a gradient: the brighter one catches the dome, the
    cornice and the minaret caps, the deeper one sits back on the body and the
    shafts. That reads as light falling from above, and unlike a gradient it
    does not turn to mud when the icon is scaled down.

    Note the crescent. Its cutting circle deliberately breaks clear through the
    right-hand edge of the outer one; sitting it wholly inside draws a ring
    with a nick in it, which is exactly what the first attempt looked like.

    The 108x108 canvas only shows its middle 72x72 once a launcher masks it, so
    nothing here strays outside a circle of radius 33 around (54,54). The
    bottom corner of a minaret is the closest call.
-->
